      "writtenOn": "2022-01-27T23:41:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like these mirror the ones in C99:\n\nhttps://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/isnan\nhttps://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/isinf\nhttps://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/fpclassify\n\nI guess we can\u0027t use them since we don\u0027t link against libc. However, let\u0027s try to maintain the same header structure, so including \"math.h\" should define these functions (not \"math_util.h\"). Our equivalent of libc headers is in \"builtin/\" directory, so this would be \"builtin/math.h\". \"builtin/math.h\" includes a core-specific fpu.h and it looks like there is an x86-specific version in \"minute-ia/include/fpu.h\": https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/c5e21a86ffd8c8e29dfb24ba88581c23acdd2f15/core/minute-ia/include/fpu.h#199. It doesn\u0027t look like that one is used anywhere, so we could probably remove it and just provide this generic version.\n\nWith this generic version, can we write a host test for isnan and isinf?\n\nLet\u0027s break this out into a separate commit for clarity.",
